          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"fixing-newlines-model-development-walkthrough\">Fixing newlines: model development walkthrough</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This notebook drives the full pipeline of the newline-fixing service \u2014\n<strong>data preparation \u2192 training \u2192 evaluation</strong> \u2014 and visualizes the results.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The task is framed as <strong>gap classification</strong>: the text is split into words, and a\nmodel predicts one of four separators between each consecutive pair \u2014\n<code>JOIN</code> (halves of one word), <code>SPACE</code>, <code>NEWLINE</code> (<code>\\n</code>), <code>PARA</code> (<code>\\n\\n</code>).\nReconstruction from words + gaps can only change whitespace, never words.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Each heavy step is gated behind a <strong>run button</strong> and shells out to the same\n<code>scripts/*.py</code> CLIs documented in <code>report.md</code>, so what you see here is exactly\nwhat a terminal run does. Cells render from artifacts on disk, so a notebook\nrestart picks up wherever the pipeline left off.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "5c528c133bff0bf1c8d21615217d1bc0",
