          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"1-data-preparation\">1 \u00b7 Data preparation</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Clean structured text is its own supervision: we record the true gap classes,\nthen destroy the newlines (and occasionally split words) to create inputs.\nSources: <strong>wikitext-103</strong> (prose + headings) and a <strong>markdown corpus</strong>\n(headings + bullet lists, like the README's arXiv example).</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Small doc counts below give a quick demo corpus; raise them for the real run\n(the full run is also fine from a terminal \u2014 the button uses the same CLI).</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
